---
import DocsLayout from '../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
---

<DocsLayout title="Thinking Budget & Modality Bridge" currentPath="/docs/guides/thinking-budget">
  <div class="space-y-8 font-mono text-xs">
    <div>
      <div class="text-[11px] text-zinc-400 font-semibold mb-1">REASONING & MULTIMODAL</div>
      <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white font-sans">Thinking Budget & Modality Bridge</h1>
      <p class="text-zinc-400 text-sm font-sans mt-1">Configuring extended reasoning budgets for Claude 3.7 Sonnet, DeepSeek R1, and Gemini 2.5.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-[#111113] border border-[#222226] space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-sm font-bold text-white font-sans">Thinking Budget Configuration</h2>
      <p class="text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
        Pass <code class="text-zinc-200">thinking: &#123; type: "enabled", budget_tokens: 4096 &#125;</code> in chat completions requests. RouteNex normalizes this parameter across Anthropic, DeepSeek, and Google reasoning adapters.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-[#111113] border border-[#222226] space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-sm font-bold text-white font-sans">Modality Bridge Fallback</h2>
      <p class="text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
        When an image or audio file is sent to a text-only target model, RouteNex automatically routes the media payload through a multimodal descriptor model first, inserting the detailed transcription or description into the message context seamlessly.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
